<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a bug in the `encode_ise` function in the project. The fuzzer generates a `quant_method` value of `QUANT_24`, which is a valid enum value but is not handled correctly by the `encode_ise` function. The function appears to fall through to the code path for `QUANT_3`, which then attempts to access the `trits_of_integer` and `integer_of_trits` arrays with out-of-bounds indices, leading to a global-buffer-overflow.

The fix for the project would be to add a `default` case to the switch statement in `encode_ise` to handle unexpected `quant_method` values gracefully, or to ensure that all possible enum values are handled correctly.

The fuzzer could also be improved by only generating `quant_method` values that are explicitly handled by the `encode_ise` function. This can be done by using `stream.PickValueInArray` with an array of valid `quant_method` values.
</crash-analysis>

